{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures","id":1164833,"title":"A Changeling and a Mage adventures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-03T10:57:24-08:00","id":1164833,"title":"A Changeling and a Mage adventures","content":"Hello everyone (wavy wavy), am having this campaign setting that involves the adventure of two awkwardly best friends ever, that go for adventures in the worlds of dreaming and beyond.<br /> The characters are a Redcap mayor of a Greek island, both in the Autumn world and the Dreaming, which means that he has two towns to take care of and a Dreamspeaker Mage who happens to have his own castle on the same island. They both help eachother to run both towns and the Mage has been accepted as honorary member of the Dream town as well.<br /> The Mage also has Fae nobility Status 4 in a fae land called The Land of Miraval (aka Miracle Valey) to which he travels with a powerful artifact ship called ''The Windborn Misstress''.<br /> <br /> So I have some questions about various stuff like<br /> <br /> a) I Gave to the Redcap a ''Mayor status'' equivalent to 3 dot Title Background since he is the voice and will of house Ailil on the major part of the island, should he have a higher Title than that of a baron-like one maintain such a position ?<br /> (I have seen a related topic that didn't help much)<br /> <br /> b)Can the freehold be an entire town? With balefires flickering upon iron torches along the roads of the town and changelings being able to use them with the mayor's permission? Sign some contracts ... erm papers please.<br /> <br /> c)Similar to the Freehold issue what level of the Holdings background would need to cover the town ? I guess a 5dot might be a must.<br /> <br /> d) The Legendary Ship with which the friends travel is a big one, since it is an entire ship, a 5 dot Mage Wonder or 5 dot Changeling Chimera, the ship is alive and is indeed a lady, with a sculpted prow to the form of a beautiful sea maiden that can turn around and show to her ''owners'' the ''middle finger'' if they make her angry.<br /> <br /> e) A mage's spirit sphere may affect chimeras in the fae assuming that they are akin to umbral world or part of it ? What about changelings themselves? The spheres that are needed to affect a Changeling may be affected by their Autumn or Chimerical state ?<br /> Eg: Mind + Spirit to affect nightmares, Matter + Spirit to affect inanimate chimeras etc etc.<br /> <br /> f) may the Redcap affect umbral entities with appropriate realms like they were chimera for the sake of crossover ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-03-2017, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T23:04:00-08:00","id":1166919,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> In my oppinion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures#post1164833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) I Gave to the Redcap a ''Mayor status'' equivalent to 3 dot Title Background since he is the voice and will of house Ailil on the major part of the island, should he have a higher Title than that of a baron-like one maintain such a position ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think check his chimerical influence. If it doesn't reach out far, give him 3, if he is well known and contacted, &amp; his holdings have some importance (docks, market, trods, Silver Gate to Whatever, booty cheerleaders, situated on a trade route), give him 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures#post1164833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b)Can the freehold be an entire town? With balefires flickering upon iron torches along the roads of the town and changelings being able to use them with the mayor's permission? Sign some contracts ... erm papers please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not reccomend the freehold to cover an entire town. The influx of banal turists, migrants, alcoholist burn out crabfishers would at least slowly wear it's force down. About the balefire: it's the spiritual essence / center / pillar of the freehold. I wouldn't divide it.<br /> Hovewer, it may be possible, especially with the help of a mage to make distortions in the space to get the balefire accessible through torches (wormholes?).<br /> But do as it fits best in your game. CtD shouldn't follow all the rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures#post1164833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c)Similar to the Freehold issue what level of the Holdings background would need to cover the town ? I guess a 5dot might be a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures#post1164833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">d) The Legendary Ship with which the friends travel is a big one, since it is an entire ship, a 5 dot Mage Wonder or 5 dot Changeling Chimera, the ship is alive and is indeed a lady, with a sculpted prow to the form of a beautiful sea maiden that can turn around and show to her ''owners'' the ''middle finger'' if they make her angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it a Chimera, with an ugly, peeled painted old rustheap (Check Kalaka ferry.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1164833-a-changeling-and-a-mage-adventures#post1164833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">e) A mage's spirit sphere may affect chimeras in the fae assuming that they are akin to umbral world or part of it ? What about changelings themselves? The spheres that are needed to affect a Changeling may be affected by their Autumn or Chimerical state ?<br /> Eg: Mind + Spirit to affect nightmares, Matter + Spirit to affect inanimate chimeras etc etc.<br /> <br /> ]f) may the Redcap affect umbral entities with appropriate realms like they were chimera for the sake of crossover ?</div> </div> </div> </div>About the spheres: Check the Book of Lost Dreams for crossover rules. About the Redcap: With fae 5, and would be able to interact with them, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T03:51:43-08:00","id":1166944,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar562_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"562\" data-vbnamecard=\"562\">Lachdanan</a> , you have been very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}